WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.129
The city should be a space of coexistence where you have everything 

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:06.548
at hand, like a city of 15 minutes.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:42.042
We made our own project for Pontevedra, 

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.835
which was a city that at that time

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:45.587
had 73,000 inhabitants. 

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:47.547
Now we have 84,000

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.631
throughout the whole municipality,

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:50.717
mostly in the center of the city,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.510
which used to be uninhabitable.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.431
It was polluted with cars, really noisy,

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:57.515
contaminated,

00:00:57.515 --> 00:01:02.395
and people had no autonomy 
to occupy any public space.

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:30.090
For that, we did a few things:

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.843
eliminate unnecessary traffic 
so that the city works.

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:35.678
Second is crosstown traffic.

00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:40.767
We had a study that said that 30% 
of the cars that cross the city

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.810
did not stop in the city.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.978
Then we had the so-called 
agitation traffic,

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:47.982
which resulted from all 
those cars circling around

00:01:47.982 --> 00:01:50.401
until a parking spot opened up.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.074
We went from 30%

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:58.701
dedicated to public space in the city

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.454
and 70% dedicated to motor traffic

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.624
to the inverse, 70% for the people

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.751
and 30% for the traffic

00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:09.212
necessary for the city to function.

00:02:09.212 --> 00:02:10.088
What happened?

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:14.843
This led to less pollution, 
less noise, less traffic jams, 

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:17.720
which after 24 years we 
have shown are very few,

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:22.058
and are perfectly compatible 
with high quality of life

00:02:22.058 --> 00:02:24.519
and above all with great economic activity,

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:26.354
and it makes the city more attractive.

00:02:26.354 --> 00:02:27.814
The people have won. 

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:32.235
It was the space that was freed from 
cars and improved and illuminated

00:02:32.235 --> 00:02:35.822
and filled with activities, etc. 
It was filled with people.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:40.201
Since 2011, we haven’t had a single 
death from a hit-and-run in the city.

00:02:54.382 --> 00:02:59.929
This street used to have back-in parking, parallel parking,

00:02:59.929 --> 00:03:02.223
sidewalks narrowed to one meter, 

00:03:02.223 --> 00:03:05.768
and cars double-parked and triple-parked.

00:03:05.768 --> 00:03:09.105
This street was absolutely unlivable

00:03:09.105 --> 00:03:11.191
and what we transformed it into is a space

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.860
with a single platform for hanging out,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.447
and it really improved a lot in every sense.

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:21.576
I know many people who come to live in Pontevedra because they have children

00:03:21.576 --> 00:03:24.829
and prefer a city with this quality 
of life over living in another city,

00:03:24.829 --> 00:03:28.333
especially people who 
can afford to telework.

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:34.047
There are even many foreigners, 
Americans, English, French,

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:38.051
that live here and work, and choose Pontevedra for its quality of life.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.574
When we talk about 
recovering public space,

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.034
we are talking about democracy,

00:04:03.034 --> 00:04:04.786
we are talking about equality,

00:04:04.786 --> 00:04:06.412
we are talking about rights,

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.707
we are talking about making 
a feminist design of public space,

00:04:09.707 --> 00:04:12.418
because women are the ones 
who use that space the most.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:15.505
We have to fight for quality of life,

00:04:15.505 --> 00:04:19.592
to avoid climate change, to improve
the autonomy of people,

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.552
to create democracy in the public space,

00:04:21.552 --> 00:04:23.888
for social cohesion, for all of that.

00:04:23.888 --> 00:04:25.014
Can there be opposition?

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:27.517
I’m not saying there can’t be, 
but citizens are smarter

00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:30.895
than some politicians think and 
they understand perfectly

00:04:30.895 --> 00:04:33.940
when you are acting in favor 
of the general interest

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:39.320
or you are defending particular and private interests that are usually the same.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:43.825
I think that it is mainly because 
people are reluctant

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:46.035
to change and afraid of 
what they might lose.

00:04:46.035 --> 00:04:47.453
When you leave your house,

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:52.083
you need to find a public space that 
is continuous with your own house,

00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:57.714
that is calm, that is safe, 
that is pleasant, that is attractive,

00:04:57.714 --> 00:05:01.509
and that has an urban design 
that can be easily read.

